WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.160
Hey. Good morning, O Sparkling One.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.100
A-Alcor!

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.350
Yes. I am the Anguished One, Alcor.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.160
Why are you here?

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:23.540
Because no one told me to go home.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.500
Have I been a bother, Sparkling One?

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.060
Do you have no green
tea, O Sparkling One?

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.480
A-All I have is coffee.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:43.960
Is that so?

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:48.360
But you've taken the time to get
it for me, so I'll drink it.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.220
Even a Septentrion drinks tea?

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.070
Yamato taught me this in his youth:

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:00.080
This is how humans make
time to discuss things.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.980
Yamato did?

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:06.860
Alcor, what is your relation to Yamato?

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.440
We were friends. At least, I think so.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.050
"Were"?

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:15.330
Even when he was just born,
he had several abilities.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.600
And choices.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.500
Being born with great power,

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.280
he'd surely make the right
decision. So I thought.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.060
You don't think so anymore?

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.290
I think it a shame he turned his back

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:32.070
on his other abilities and
made a choice so quickly.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:34.810
What is Yamato's choice?

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.350
To oversee the talented humans.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.620
A world that is a meritocracy.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.850
That's fine in and of itself.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.080
It's not fine at all!

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.190
Who's talented and who's weak?

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.350
Who gets to decide that?

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.160
It seems Yamato Hotsuin can.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.590
He lacks the hesitation of other humans.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.830
I don't intend to agree or object

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:59.440
to the choice humans have made.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:03.020
But being obstinate, denying
possibility is denying thought.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:04.600
It's not pretty.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.290
So, we should think of another way?

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.940
Is that it, perhaps?

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:11.950
Hibiki.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:15.640
You were born with tremendous power.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.070
I never wanted it.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.430
That's how talent is.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.890
Whether it's wanted or
not makes no difference.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.560
And now... You continue
to worry over it.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:30.400
So long as you keep thinking,
you will have a choice.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.960
I'm sure there's a good one.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.970
Coffee certainly is bitter.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.110
So you taste, too.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.890
Want to add some sugar?

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.280
Let's try.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.490
I like it better this way.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.100
Thank, you, Hibiki.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.390
It was no big deal.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:12.460
Your giving me a choice let me
make this drink to my liking.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.840
Hibiki, that's what makes possibilities.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.500
Say, Alcor...

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.780
Can't you help humanity?

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.870
I'm a mechanism created by Polaris.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.360
I can't directly oppose.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.360
This is what I am.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.290
Oh, that's right.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.550
All I can do is look on.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.170
So, you're staying in my room?

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.890
Where else should I go?

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.870
I don't know.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.020
You don't, eh?

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.800
What have you done so far?

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.790
I've anguished.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.380
Because I can do nothing.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:57.000
I am a mechanism that
developed emotions.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:00.560
Just what am I?

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.000
Alcor...

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.000
If you're not our enemy...

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.460
If you won't interfere,
then you can stay here.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:22.070
It seems your perception
of me has changed somewhat.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:23.570
Well...

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.100
Given the time to talk, anyone would.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.000
Your understanding has
furthered our relationship.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.900
I'm happy, Sparkling One.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:37.510
Just what are the Septentriones?

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:41.490
But you can't let anyone find you.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.730
If anyone knew a Septentrion were here,

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:45.400
it would start a war.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.260
I'll make sure not to be found out.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.290
Please do.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.140
Hibiki, you awake?

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.960
Shijima, knock knock!

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.810
Whoa, hey now.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.670
So, about what's next--

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:59.170
Hello, humans.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.650
I can explain!

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:01.990
Th-That's...!

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:04.910
Wait, Nitta!

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.550
Please listen!

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:07.390
B-But...

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.970
Hibiki! That's that
weird dude from before!

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:11.290
Daichi, calm down.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.020
So, now what?

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.580
You've come to kill Hibiki, you demon?!

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.860
I'm telling you, I'm not a demon.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:23.260
A Septentrion?

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.130
Seems like it.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:26.970
A minion of the invaders?!

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.490
So, he's not human?

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:29.700
Yeah.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.410
The ideals of "enemy"
and "ally" all depend on

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:33.600
your point of view.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.540
Alcor, you be quiet.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:36.920
Why?

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.460
It'll make things difficult.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:39.570
Oh, really?

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:43.280
Look, he's not an enemy we have to beat.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:44.760
I think.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:45.590
That's right.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:48.140
Alcor, you be quiet.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:48.780
Oh, really?

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:50.400
For real?

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.430
Still, when you put it like that...

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:53.750
What about the others?

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:56.020
We're the only ones who know.

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:58.610
I don't want any hijinks
to spread confusion.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.210
Yeah.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.870
Daichi, will you trust me with this

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.680
till you can make a proper judgment?

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:06.780
Uh, yeah.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.320
Hibiki, you're so wise.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:09.870
You're an idiot, aren't you?

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:12.140
Uh, you two are pretty close, huh?

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.000
Um...

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.760
What is it, Io Nitta?

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:18.590
Uh, well...

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:22.770
That is... You're floating a little.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.190
Oh, you're right.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:27.550
I do sometimes float.

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.070
You really aren't human, are you?

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:33.450
Alcor, humans keep their
feet on the ground.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.840
If you say so, I'll comply.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:39.230
You all right? Your face looks pale.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.670
I-I'm fine.

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.900
Is he really all right? That red dude...

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.880
We have to hang tough.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:51.530
Walking on the ground
is a difficult task.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.260
So THIS is a Septentrion, huh?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.620
Y-Yeah.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.860
I was about to grow worried as to

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:01.070
which leg, right or left,
with which to start walking.

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:03.710
Decisions... Possibilities...

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:08.380
We have to choose the proper
path, not be too hasty.

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:11.890
But...

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:15.910
Who can tell what's
right in this situation?

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.380
Just three more.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:32.910
Then everything in this useless
world will be finished.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.390
And then it begins.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.540
The proper world.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.100
Oh. Ban!

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:57.640
Kujo. You're being flippant.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.160
Fine, Ban.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.150
That's even MORE flippant? What?

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:04.110
Don't look so scary.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.110
It's a waste of a pretty face.

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:09.740
It's stranger to be like you,
smiling at a time like this.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:12.850
At times like this, it's
important to laugh.

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:17.140
It's too bad what happened at Nagoya.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:19.460
That's not for you to worry about.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.130
Ban, ya can't lose hope.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.110
No way!

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:26.380
We're here.

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:27.930
What gives?

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:30.280
Makoto, we're the only ones called?

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:31.630
Thank you.

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:34.780
We'll need your powers
for the mission to come.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.260
Mission?

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:39.310
The fifth Septentrion
will soon manifest.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:40.930
The enemy!

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:45.210
And? It's gotta be me and Airi, huh?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:46.790
That's right.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.670
Sometimes, summoning a specific demon

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:51.880
hinges on an individual's aptitude.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.530
Thanks to the data from
yesterday's tests,

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:59.390
we know you two are most
suited for this mission.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.050
How crappy.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:04.490
So you checked us without
givin' out the reason why?

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:06.000
There was no need to say.

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:11.010
Beatin' enemies with my own
hands actually suits me fine.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.180
So, what should we do?

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.780
Am I being watched?

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.330
That's not exactly it.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.890
It's just, we can't leave you be.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.190
But it's about time.

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:27.340
Are you fine being here?

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:28.440
Time?

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:29.170
For what?

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:31.240
The past and the future.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:34.740
Everything is ordained by providence.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:45.470
Why do only Hinako and Airi attack,

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:47.940
and all of us stay on standby?

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:52.130
The fifth Septentrion, Alioth,
will manifest in the ionosphere.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:56.460
The demons you all use
can't attack that far.

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:57.950
The ionosphere?

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:01.540
We'll launch a long-range
intercept attack.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.620
Human hands shall recreate myth.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:07.790
Yamato...

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:11.280
Alert! Septentrion
manifestation is confirmed!

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.570
Measuring enemy matter.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.780
It seems completely different!

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:17.240
Just how big can it be?

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.440
Alioth has appeared!

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:22.850
Max speed is approximately
130 kilometers!

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.850
Irrelevant. We know its location.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:29.610
The enemy is above Sapporo.

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.010
It's cold!

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:00.090
Sure enough, Hokkaido chills ya!

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:17.500
This is JP's Sapporo Branch.

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:19.030
Mission prep is complete!

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:20.610
Sapporo?

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.260
Prep is okay.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:23.240
Here, too.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.080
Hinako! Airi!

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:28.580
Oh, Hibiki. Leave this to us.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:32.590
Today's not your turn.
WE'RE gonna finish this.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:35.360
Begin mission. End communications.

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:37.110
Gotcha. Let's go.

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:39.720
Keep dinner warm for us.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.410
Makoto!

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.160
They're both fine.

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:46.640
We can use the transport Terminal
to quickly get them out of there.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:49.390
Both of them...

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.820
Begin status.

00:11:56.840 --> 00:12:00.860
Shiva is a god of destruction,
for the most part uncontrollable,

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:03.350
but it has some welcoming qualities.

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:07.330
Hinako Kujo is the sole daughter
of the Kujo family style of dance.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:12.110
She was diagnosed to have an
overwhelmingly higher aptitude

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:14.110
than the dancers prepared by JP's.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:28.300
The other, Kama, is a charming
demon who prefers young girls.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:31.440
Airi Ban was chosen via
the compatibility tests.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:34.250
There's no accounting
for a demon's tastes.

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:38.340
Th-This is no big deal!

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:49.290
Kama was successfully summoned.

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:53.420
Shiva was successfully summoned!

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.170
Guide Shiva and Kama into position.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:04.930
Alioth power is increasing!

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:06.630
Detecting an attack!

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:12.100
Deploy all Sapporo Branch
defensive barriers!

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.520
Repel Alioth's attack!

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.020
Understood. Open all Ryumyaku circuits.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:17.920
Deploy all defensive barriers!

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:31.450
Kama and Shiva are
fixed in firing range.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:32.680
Shiva.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:36.420
This demon is one of charm, who
would destroy your meditation.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:37.960
Draw upon that anger...

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:39.420
And break free!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.300
Shiva is releasing Paspata!

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:56.770
Paspata is reaching the ionosphere.

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:01.980
Direct core hit!

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:11.270
Core readings have disappeared.

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:12.290
It was a success!

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:16.540
A success, huh?

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:24.550
I see. So that's how it's done.

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:33.970
We'll soon be returning via
the transport Terminal.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.030
Understood. Proceed to Gate 3.

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:40.020
Huh? What’s that?

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:46.970
A large mass has been
confirmed above Sapporo.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:48.570
It's Alioth's shell!

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:51.850
It's falling toward Sapporo!

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:56.640
Alioth wasn't destroyed?

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:58.670
Well, the core was destroyed.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:03.170
But the shell remained.
It'll hit the ground.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.550
That's the characteristic
of the fifth Septentrion.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:09.910
Ground cameras have confirmed
the shell in mid-air.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:12.560
Volume is 500 cubic kilometers!

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:15.830
How is evacuation of the Sapporo Branch?

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:17.790
Complete for all building personnel.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.310
That leaves the staff
at the special site.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.460
Have them hurry!

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:26.380
That's the shell? It's way too big!

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:29.200
Miss Kujo, hurry and escape!

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:32.200
The city... The city will be crushed!

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:35.750
Evacuation of all staff complete!

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:51.050
Alioth is falling toward Sapporo!

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:52.620
Visual confirmation impossible.

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:54.200
Here comes a magical attack!

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:02.150
Is the tower undamaged?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:05.520
Y-Yes. Sapporo Tower detected.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:11.890
The townspeople...

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:16.350
Unfortunately, we can't
take in all the civilians.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:20.560
The situation has ended.

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:23.500
Yamato... You knew!

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:27.490
Yes. I knew the enemy's capability.

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:30.380
If you think there was
another way, say so.

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:37.530
Humanity has nowhere to run.

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:41.370
Yes. The Void is expanding.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.610
There's nowhere in the world to run.

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:46.590
Two more days.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:50.400
Will even a single human survive?

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.680
Or will no one?

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:56.440
The promised day.

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:58.300
The Septentrion onslaught.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.080
The world's transformation.

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:04.500
The Hotsuin family has known
of this for hundreds of years.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:08.100
Together with the policymakers,
they hid this,

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:09.670
wanting to attain power.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:14.660
Yamato Hotsuin wants to survive
the promised seven days,

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:16.210
create a new world that

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:20.680
follows a "national refinement
curriculum" of government design.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.420
"You just turn your
backs on us civilians?"

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:26.690
Well, the world ain't fair
at all right now, huh?

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.120
Hibiki.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:30.940
Please, don't make the wrong decision.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:34.540
I live while everyone else dies.

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:39.540
I have to shoulder all
that, and survive.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:56.820
What's wrong?

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.930
This feast was especially prepared.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:02.220
"Feast" actually sounds
kinda scary, huh?

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:03.790
Like a last supper?

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:05.920
Hey, cut that out.

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:10.270
So, sir, why'd you hold a
banquet all of a sudden?

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:14.760
Alioth was defeated thanks
to you and Airi Ban.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:15.970
This is a modest--

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:19.450
I just can't get in the mood for food.

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:22.880
Sapporo disappeared right
in front of our eyes!

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:26.650
This... What is this even for?

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:28.960
It won't make the dead any happier.

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:35.320
You can't shoulder it all, eh?

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:36.720
What do you mean?

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:39.880
Surviving means continuing
to shoulder one's burden.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:42.930
When you can't handle that strain...

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:45.230
Then next, YOU shall die.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:46.770
Yeah, right!

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.410
I'll fight tomorrow and
the day after that!

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:52.940
Airi. You have to eat.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:55.240
I prefer chawanmushi.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:57.360
I'll make some later.

00:18:58.090 --> 00:18:59.370
And you, Yamato?

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:01.830
You can shoulder the burden?

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:05.750
Of course. I've never
once thought it a burden.

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:08.700
Humans feel sadness and anger.

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.960
A wounded heart needs time to heal.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:12.590
It's a waste of time.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:16.670
Not everyone is like you,
able to be so matter-of-fact!

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:20.930
Then you should accept that
weakness and obey the stronger.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.830
But... That's a world without kindness!

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:25.100
Nitta.

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:27.620
What is kindness?

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:31.290
Is kindness being complacent,
licking one other's wounds?

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:34.740
Have you considered that while
you sleepwalk like that,

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:39.260
the incompetent trash
shall rot the world?

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:41.870
S-Stop it.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:42.990
Well?

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:46.390
What is the real reason
you've assembled us all?

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:51.630
To ask you who've survived
thus far your decision.

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:53.250
Decision?

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:57.260
The enemy invasion will end in two days.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.550
After... two days.

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:03.630
So we can finally go back home, huh?

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.200
I'd like that.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:06.740
Therein lies the problem.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:10.500
After we've defeated
the last Septentrion,

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.770
the surviving humans can meet Polaris.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:15.440
Polaris?

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:18.720
The almighty one that
governs the natural order.

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:21.430
What? The enemy has a big boss?

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:23.060
Polaris is the Answerer

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:25.390
of cause and effect,
that which sees past

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:26.700
, present and future.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.560
Uh, so it's God?

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:29.770
Shijima.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:32.770
If that is your worthless fear,
then consider it as such.

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:33.880
The heck?

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:36.090
So we'll have peace once we beat it?

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:38.190
If we did that to the Observer,

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:40.520
the world would plunge into chaos.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:43.840
Still, I think that'd be fun.

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:46.950
JP's wants to encounter Polaris,

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:51.230
and via the coefficients and
formulae that shape the world,

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:53.100
create the new order it desires.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:53.970
That's right.

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:56.070
Guess you're not a total idiot.

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.440
Wh-What's...?

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:58.440
That?

00:20:58.710 --> 00:21:03.390
They're trying to rewrite the
world into a form that suits them.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:07.260
Ronaldo knew that and
tried to stop JP's.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:12.950
So, the wishes of those who
survive will be fulfilled?

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.380
If so, then the dead...

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:16.450
Who can say?

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:19.050
If one were able to make such a

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:21.890
benevolent choice known
to Polaris, perhaps.

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:24.180
Still, this world is being attacked

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:27.000
because it's been considered irrelevant.

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:31.390
Oh, no. Some new world is just scary!

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:32.560
Nitta.

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:37.410
The world's "update" is shaped

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:39.660
by the wills of the
humans who intervene.

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:43.170
Then, the plan that the
government and the Hotsuins

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:45.320
have had for centuries will be complete.

00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:48.180
Isn't that right, Yamato?!

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:50.790
Hibiki.

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:53.210
This has nothing to do
with some "Hotsuin plan."

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:57.420
To this day, I have
lived by my own will.

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:00.920
The refuse shall not be
allowed to stop Polaris.

00:22:01.610 --> 00:22:04.280
I shall rewrite the natural
order of the world.

00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:08.300
A new world were those
of talent shall govern.

00:22:10.340 --> 00:22:13.920
And now, everyone here knows it all.

00:22:15.710 --> 00:22:20.310
In two days, those who
don't obey me may die.

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:24.560
Everyone, think long and
hard on this tonight.

00:22:31.430 --> 00:22:32.480
Yamato!

00:22:36.730 --> 00:22:39.170
Your ideals may be correct...

00:22:39.730 --> 00:22:41.280
But they're too rigid!

00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:44.760
I can't think people can be happy
in a cold future like that!

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:48.030
There's no need for you to understand.

00:22:48.030 --> 00:22:50.410
I'm simply saying what I shall do so.

00:22:50.740 --> 00:22:52.880
Those who oppose me are unnecessary.

00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:55.350
I care not if you call me an enemy.

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:57.270
I shall bring you to submission.

00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:00.940
Why are you so unable
to accept humanity?

00:23:01.890 --> 00:23:03.650
You shoulder anything and everything.

00:23:03.920 --> 00:23:07.030
Shouldering is different
from accepting, Yamato.

00:23:10.050 --> 00:23:11.660
You are naïve.

00:23:14.850 --> 00:23:18.510
Hibiki. You will stay at
my side until the end.

00:23:18.900 --> 00:23:21.260
If you're saying my existence is a sin,

00:23:21.260 --> 00:23:23.130
then you shall pass judgment.

00:23:23.410 --> 00:23:26.340
Can you promise that, Hibiki Kuze?

00:23:28.490 --> 00:23:31.160
It's a promise, Yamato.

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:35.430
Two more days.

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:39.960
If we can survive,
this will all be over.

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:44.320
But I... I don't need some new world.

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:46.220
I want to go home!

00:23:49.970 --> 00:23:50.740
Yes?

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:55.180
Makoto?

00:24:00.100 --> 00:24:02.150
Please tell me what this is about.

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:05.190
Tomorrow's mission has been decided.

00:24:05.650 --> 00:24:07.780
Io Nitta. Tomorrow...

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:09.470
You'll die for us.
